course: dictionary
lesson: 1718
title: Circumstance and its meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A circumstance is a fact or condition around an event that can change what happens. When you meet this word, read the words around it to find the clue. «Under no circumstances should you open the door to strangers.» The word no is the clue: it tells you that circumstances here means a situation where something must never happen.
explain: Circumstances can also mean someone's situation, especially how much money they have. «In reduced circumstances» means poorer than before, and «in straitened circumstances» means poor and short of money. Both phrases are old-fashioned, so a friend might say «hard up» or «a bit short» instead.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Under no circumstances» becomes «never», and the sentence still makes sense, so you have the right meaning. Phrases such as «in the circumstances» mean because of the situation, so read the whole sentence before you decide.
fact: Circumstances means the facts or conditions around an event that affect what happens.
fact: «Under no circumstances» means never, not at all.
fact: «In reduced circumstances» means poorer than before; «in straitened circumstances» means poor and short of money.
fact: Someone's circumstances can mean their situation, especially how much money they have.
fact: «In the circumstances» means because of the situation.
exercise: «Under no circumstances should you open the door to strangers.» What does under no circumstances mean? | Sometimes, if you feel like it | Only on Sundays | *Never, not at all | Quickly, before dinner
exercise: «The family was in reduced circumstances after the factory closed.» What does in reduced circumstances mean? | Living in a big house | Richer than before | Tired from a long walk | *Poorer than before
exercise: A friend says «a bit short» where an old-fashioned speaker would say «in straitened circumstances». What does it mean? | Short of time for a holiday | *Short of money | Short in height | Short of breath after running
test: «Because of the circumstances, the picnic was moved indoors.» What does circumstances mean here? | Pieces of cake | A kind of tent | *The situation, such as the weather | The name of a park
test: «Under the circumstances, Ella decided to stay home.» What does under the circumstances suggest? | At a party | Happily, for no reason | Against the law | *Because of the situation
exam: Which phrase means poor and short of money? | *in straitened circumstances | under no circumstances | due to circumstances | in the circumstances
